# Cursor AI Rules for Wishlist Project

## Documentation

See `.cursorrules-docs.md` for comprehensive documentation guidelines.

## Code Quality Guidelines

### General Principles

- Prefer TypeScript strict mode
- Use meaningful variable names
- Keep functions small and focused
- Write self-documenting code with clear names
- Add comments for complex logic only

### File Organization

- Components in `/src/components`
- API routes in `/src/app/api`
- Utilities in `/src/lib`
- Hooks in `/src/hooks`
- Types should be co-located with their usage

### React Components

- Use TypeScript for all components
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use proper prop typing
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks

### API Routes

- Always validate input
- Return structured error responses
- Use proper HTTP status codes
- Log errors with context
- Include proper TypeScript types

## Testing & Deployment

### Before Committing

- Run linting: `bun run lint`
- Fix formatting: `bun run format`
- Test the feature manually
- Remove console.logs (except for important server logs)

### Commit Messages

- Use conventional commits format
- Be descriptive but concise
- Reference issue numbers when applicable
- Examples:
  - `feat: add gift exchange feature`
  - `fix: resolve smart account auth issue`
  - `docs: update Redis caching guide`
  - `refactor: consolidate wishlist utilities`

## Environment Variables

### Required for Development

- Always update `env.example` when adding new variables
- Never commit `.env.local`
- Document what each variable is for in setup guides
- Use descriptive variable names

## AI Assistant Behavior

### When Working on Tasks

- Read existing code before suggesting changes
- Check for existing patterns and follow them
- Update documentation if you change implementation
- Clean up temporary files after debugging
- Ask for clarification on ambiguous requirements

### When Creating Documentation

- Check `/docs/README.md` first to avoid duplication
- Follow the documentation format guidelines above
- Only create docs that will have long-term value
- Update the index when adding new docs

